    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryce Harper** (76.31) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (73.30) represent our clear offensive anchors. **Bryce Harper** draws a favorable matchup against a struggling J. Kent, and with his elite xwOBA metrics paired with the favorable park factors and high-leverage order position, he is the primary engine of our lineup. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** exploits a high-floor matchup against a left-handed arm, benefiting from consistent run-production opportunities in the two-hole. **Cal Raleigh** (68.23) also grades out as a premier play; he catches a vulnerable arm in R. Johnson, and despite the slight dynamic platoon tax, the matchup against a 5.18 xERA starter makes him an essential start behind the plate.\n\nWe are paying close attention to speed-reliant options, as **Jung Hoo Lee** (60.52) has been elevated due to the pitcher's slow delivery, which significantly boosts his stolen base potential today. Conversely, **Jeremiah Jackson** (46.70) remains our most marginal start; while he is currently in the lineup, his low ceiling against a sub-4.00 xERA arm makes him a candidate for mid-game substitution if we need to prioritize defensive efficiency or late-inning pivots. **Gleyber Torres** (50.45) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine, but he ultimately hit the bench due to a significant negative platoon adjustment against R. Fisher, which pushed his efficiency rating below the threshold of our current outfield and utility starters.\n\nWe are monitoring the overall volatility of the day, particularly regarding potential weather-related delays or late lineup shifts that could affect our lower-tier starters. While we feel confident in the daily efficiency scores, the margin between **Kyle Karros** (57.41) and our bench remains thin. Provided the weather holds, we expect **Alex Freeland** and **Masyn Winn** to provide enough utility in the middle infield to keep us competitive in the stolen base category, provided their favorable SP skill matchups translate into consistent on-base opportunities.",
